From: openSUSE Publishing <publishing@opensuse.org>
Subject: [PATCH] No self-update in distro builds: no startup check, no install prompt
Bug: none (downstream distribution policy, not upstreamable)

The package manager owns updates on a distro install: do not phone
home to the releases page on every GUI launch, and never offer to
install an upstream release (UPDATE-AND-RESTART) over RPM-owned
files. Upstream ships this machinery intentionally for its own
builds. Help ▸ Check for Updates stays as an explicit manual action
reporting through its outcome window; only the automatic startup
check and the self-update install prompt are turned off.

diff --git a/apps/filmcraft/src/main.rs b/apps/filmcraft/src/main.rs
--- a/apps/filmcraft/src/main.rs
+++ b/apps/filmcraft/src/main.rs
@@ -254,7 +254,10 @@
             }
         }
         let mut app = FilmcraftApp::new(session);
-        app.set_startup_update_check(true);
+        // Downstream (openSUSE): the package manager owns updates, so the
+        // desktop app must not check for (and offer to install) upstream
+        // releases on its own at startup. Manual Help ▸ Check stays.
+        app.set_startup_update_check(false);
         app.graphics_notice = notice;
         if recover == Some(false) {
             app.dialog = None;
